<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>News on PacoChan's Website</title><link>https://pacochan.net/posts/</link><description>Recent content in News on PacoChan's Website</description><generator>Hugo -- gohugo.io</generator><language>en</language><copyright>© 2026 PacoChan</copyright><lastBuildDate>Thu, 26 Mar 2026 02:51:28 +0100</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://pacochan.net/posts/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>New 1.2 version of the Banjo-Kazooie Spanish translation</title><link>https://pacochan.net/posts/2026-03-26-banjo-kazooie-translation-1-2/</link><pubDate>Thu, 26 Mar 2026 02:51:28 +0100</pubDate><guid>https://pacochan.net/posts/2026-03-26-banjo-kazooie-translation-1-2/</guid><description>Thirteen years later, and thanks to the big advances made in game decompilation, I’ve taken advantage of the fact that the source code for Banjo-Kazooie is now available to improve the translation.</description><media:content xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" url="https://pacochan.net/posts/2026-03-26-banjo-kazooie-translation-1-2/feature-background.jpg"/></item><item><title>Server Shenanigans</title><link>https://pacochan.net/posts/2025-12-17-server-shenanigans/</link><pubDate>Wed, 17 Dec 2025 06:49:50 +0100</pubDate><guid>https://pacochan.net/posts/2025-12-17-server-shenanigans/</guid><description>Over the last few days, I&amp;rsquo;ve been busy reinstalling everything on my VPS because it turns out that it got infected due to a vulnerability in React Server Components that affected Next.js, among other things.</description><media:content xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" url="https://pacochan.net/posts/2025-12-17-server-shenanigans/feature-background.jpg"/></item><item><title>Messing around with a Bluetooth printer</title><link>https://pacochan.net/posts/2025-03-08-messing-around-with-a-bluetooth-printer/</link><pubDate>Sat, 08 Mar 2025 20:00:20 +0100</pubDate><guid>https://pacochan.net/posts/2025-03-08-messing-around-with-a-bluetooth-printer/</guid><description>I recently acquired one of these thermal printers to be able to print small labels quickly. And since I didn&amp;rsquo;t find any open source alternative that would work for me, I wanted to try to do my own program as a fun challenge.</description><media:content xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" url="https://pacochan.net/posts/2025-03-08-messing-around-with-a-bluetooth-printer/feature-background.jpg"/></item><item><title>Finished a Perfect Dark save editor</title><link>https://pacochan.net/posts/2024-08-19-finished-pd-save-editor/</link><pubDate>Mon, 19 Aug 2024 11:33:23 +0200</pubDate><guid>https://pacochan.net/posts/2024-08-19-finished-pd-save-editor/</guid><description>Being my favorite game, I had long wanted to make a Perfect Dark save editor. Mainly to see and understand what information is hidden inside a save file.</description><media:content xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" url="https://pacochan.net/posts/2024-08-19-finished-pd-save-editor/feature-background.jpg"/></item><item><title>New comments system</title><link>https://pacochan.net/posts/2023-10-20-new-comments-system/</link><pubDate>Fri, 20 Oct 2023 19:33:04 +0200</pubDate><guid>https://pacochan.net/posts/2023-10-20-new-comments-system/</guid><description>After renovating the site a few months ago I mentioned that I wasn&amp;rsquo;t sure how to implement the comments system, since the site is now totally static. After a lot of research and trying different solutions, I ended up using a &lt;em&gt;selfhosted&lt;/em&gt; comments system called Remark42.</description><media:content xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" url="https://pacochan.net/posts/2023-10-20-new-comments-system/feature-background.jpg"/></item><item><title>Added Resident Evil - Text Adventure</title><link>https://pacochan.net/posts/2023-08-29-added-re-text-adventure/</link><pubDate>Tue, 29 Aug 2023 15:39:59 +0200</pubDate><guid>https://pacochan.net/posts/2023-08-29-added-re-text-adventure/</guid><description>If you have played and completed Without Escape, you may have seen in the extras section an option called &lt;em&gt;Background&lt;/em&gt; where I explain where the idea of making the game initially came from.</description><media:content xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" url="https://pacochan.net/posts/2023-08-29-added-re-text-adventure/feature-background.jpg"/></item><item><title>Finished a Banjo-Kazooie save editor</title><link>https://pacochan.net/posts/2023-08-12-finished-bk-save-editor/</link><pubDate>Sat, 12 Aug 2023 04:42:30 +0200</pubDate><guid>https://pacochan.net/posts/2023-08-12-finished-bk-save-editor/</guid><description>As I mentioned when I finished my Super Mario 64 save editor, I was interested in making one for Banjo-Kazooie.</description><media:content xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" url="https://pacochan.net/posts/2023-08-12-finished-bk-save-editor/feature-background.jpg"/></item><item><title>Finished a Super Mario 64 save editor</title><link>https://pacochan.net/posts/2023-07-29-finished-sm64-save-editor/</link><pubDate>Sat, 29 Jul 2023 14:44:52 +0200</pubDate><guid>https://pacochan.net/posts/2023-07-29-finished-sm64-save-editor/</guid><description>Time ago I did a save editor for Super Mario 64, but it was exclusive for Windows and I never published it. I decided to rewrite it from scratch, improve it, and make it cross-platform.</description><media:content xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" url="https://pacochan.net/posts/2023-07-29-finished-sm64-save-editor/feature-background.png"/></item><item><title>A decade later... new website... again</title><link>https://pacochan.net/posts/2023-05-23-new-page-decade-later/</link><pubDate>Tue, 23 May 2023 21:43:59 +0200</pubDate><guid>https://pacochan.net/posts/2023-05-23-new-page-decade-later/</guid><description/><media:content xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" url="https://pacochan.net/posts/2023-05-23-new-page-decade-later/feature-background.jpg"/></item><item><title>Banjo-Kazooie Editor version 1.4</title><link>https://pacochan.net/posts/2014-01-19-banjo-kazooie-editor-version-1-4/</link><pubDate>Sun, 19 Jan 2014 18:55:52 +0200</pubDate><guid>https://pacochan.net/posts/2014-01-19-banjo-kazooie-editor-version-1-4/</guid><description>I’ve made another update to the editor. The main chage is that the program is able to import correctly TGA files with modified resolution.</description><media:content xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" url="https://pacochan.net/posts/2014-01-19-banjo-kazooie-editor-version-1-4/feature-background.jpg"/></item><item><title>Banjo-Kazooie Editor version 1.3</title><link>https://pacochan.net/posts/2013-11-06-banjo-kazooie-editor-version-1-3/</link><pubDate>Wed, 06 Nov 2013 16:24:56 +0200</pubDate><guid>https://pacochan.net/posts/2013-11-06-banjo-kazooie-editor-version-1-3/</guid><description>I’ve made another update to the editor. The main chage is that the big font used in some menus of the game is now editable.</description><media:content xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" url="https://pacochan.net/posts/2013-11-06-banjo-kazooie-editor-version-1-3/feature-background.jpg"/></item><item><title>Banjo-Kazooie Editor version 1.2</title><link>https://pacochan.net/posts/2013-09-01-banjo-kazooie-editor-version-1-2/</link><pubDate>Sun, 01 Sep 2013 11:25:18 +0200</pubDate><guid>https://pacochan.net/posts/2013-09-01-banjo-kazooie-editor-version-1-2/</guid><description>This time I’ve made a very interesting update to the editor.</description><media:content xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" url="https://pacochan.net/posts/2013-09-01-banjo-kazooie-editor-version-1-2/feature-background.jpg"/></item><item><title>Banjo-Kazooie Spanish translation update</title><link>https://pacochan.net/posts/2013-09-01-banjo-kazooie-translation-update/</link><pubDate>Sun, 01 Sep 2013 11:11:49 +0200</pubDate><guid>https://pacochan.net/posts/2013-09-01-banjo-kazooie-translation-update/</guid><description>After four years since the release of the first version, here&amp;rsquo;s an update.</description><media:content xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" url="https://pacochan.net/posts/2013-09-01-banjo-kazooie-translation-update/feature-background.jpg"/></item><item><title>Banjo-Kazooie Editor version 1.1</title><link>https://pacochan.net/posts/2013-08-22-banjo-kazooie-editor-version-1-1/</link><pubDate>Thu, 22 Aug 2013 17:45:31 +0200</pubDate><guid>https://pacochan.net/posts/2013-08-22-banjo-kazooie-editor-version-1-1/</guid><description>I’ve updated this program because one user found a problem while editing the font.</description><media:content xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" url="https://pacochan.net/posts/2013-08-22-banjo-kazooie-editor-version-1-1/feature-background.jpg"/></item><item><title>New website... again!</title><link>https://pacochan.net/posts/2012-02-13-new-website-again/</link><pubDate>Mon, 13 Feb 2012 19:14:47 +0200</pubDate><guid>https://pacochan.net/posts/2012-02-13-new-website-again/</guid><description/><media:content xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" url="https://pacochan.net/posts/2012-02-13-new-website-again/feature-background.jpg"/></item><item><title>Finished Mario Party translation</title><link>https://pacochan.net/posts/2011-09-22-finished-mario-party-translation/</link><pubDate>Thu, 22 Sep 2011 17:33:25 +0200</pubDate><guid>https://pacochan.net/posts/2011-09-22-finished-mario-party-translation/</guid><description/><media:content xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" url="https://pacochan.net/posts/2011-09-22-finished-mario-party-translation/feature-background.jpg"/></item><item><title>I have finally finished Without Escape</title><link>https://pacochan.net/posts/2011-08-03-finally-finished-without-escape/</link><pubDate>Wed, 03 Aug 2011 00:42:10 +0200</pubDate><guid>htt